<title>SPAIN: PESETA DEBT/INTERBANK CLOSING REPORT.</title>
<headline>PESETA DEBT/INTERBANK CLOSING REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds drifted lower into the close on Thursday, trailing German Bund futures as dollar/mark concerns continued to plague the market, dealers said.</p>
<p>Trade focused on futures, with very little turnover in the cash market. Dealers said trade had been mostly technical with a lack of domestic news to provide inspiration.</p>
<p>&quot;The market is making limited technical moves in futures, and there was practically no activity in cash,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>Dealers expected the market's direction to remain hooked to Bunds and dollar/mark for now.</p>
</text>
